<title>BRAZIL: Brazil authorizes 7.35 pct increase in air fares.</title>
<headline>Brazil authorizes 7.35 pct increase in air fares.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Finance Ministry has authorized airline companies to raise their ticket prices by a maximum of 7.35 percent, the ministry said Thursday.</p>
<p>The increases, the first since June 1996, may come into effect July 21, the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>The government was seeking to gradually deregulate Brazil's airline industry but would introduce measures to ensure competition in the sector, the statement said.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 3141193))</p>
